candidate_text:
Position: Business Analyst
Moreinfo: Responsibilities: 

• Managing product requirements and product backlog throughout the whole requirements lifecycle;
• Identifying stakeholders, providing expectation management, negotiating and allocating scope based on business needs and constraints; • Acting as proxy product owner: communicating, prioritizing and validating requirements with all relevant stakeholders; • Eliciting and modeling business, product, functional and non-functional requirements into detailed user stories ready for development and other supplementary documentation (Value Stream, Business Objective Model); • Assisting UX designer in screen mockups creation, checking design for missing requirements; • Tracking scope and managing requirements change requests; • Conducting acceptance testing and demos for Clients.

Achievements:
• Experienced working with a multi scrum team (30+), successfully facilitated meetings and supported project team on all stages of product development;
• Established strong relationships and informatively communicated development decisions with project’s key stakeholders;
• Collaborated with all relevant stakeholders to get a better understanding of the Business Processes and, as a result, to meet specific technical and business needs; • Negotiated and allocated scope within business needs and delivery date/budget constraints;
• Analyzed competitors and provided research to improve product’s user experience;
• Improved and initialized processes setup in project development team based on the best practices, assisted in resource workload management.
Looking For: Interested in new international projects with a great team. Open to Product manager position as well. Willing to learn new skills, languages and obtain appropriate certifications.
English Level: fluent
Experience Years: 1.5
