candidate_text:
Position: Business Analyst
Moreinfo: I started my way in IT from sales and marketing, however, in a short time, switched to project and product management. Also, I have an experience in a startup and I know how to manage ideas from scratch. I worked with different domains (such as e-commerce, marketplaces, advertising, b2b2c projects, Web 3.0, etc) and different teams. So, my wide experience makes me efficient in product development and helps to provide an excellent level of service to the company that hires me.

As a result, I excel at:
- Product vision and Road Map maintenance;
- Market research and Competitor analysis;
- Agile and Scrum processes integration and the following;
- UX wireframes and the designer management;
- User Stories, Use Cases and JTBD;
- Customer Journey Maps and Personas;
- Writing technical documentation and UML diagrams, etc;
- Management of projects on MVP and PoC phases;
- Backlog and requirements management;
- Product measurements and improvements;
- In-time deliveries and delivery impact tracking;

I know how to build and manage teams in the right way, communicate with different levels of stakeholders (from meetings with founders and investors to interviews with end users) and align their expectations. And how to find insights and bring valuable features to the market, track their impact and build a new list of improvements for future releases.

In addition, I have experience in programming, business analysis and UX design. This knowledge helps me be at the front of discussions and do the talking as equals to technical and business interlocutors or build a bridge between them.
