Position: CTO, Team Lead, Project Manager
Moreinfo: Data analysis suits:  R, octave, matlab,  numpy
AI frameworks: Orange, scikits, tensorflow

Research : 
Biophysics, electrophysiology, cell culture, protein extraction, microscopy, Ca2+ imaging, Computational Physics, modeling, MD simulation

Programming languages :
Ada, C/C++,  Delphi/Pascal, Java, Python, Prolog
Looking For: Accomplished scientist and software developer with management experience (Professor, CTO). California Institute of Technology graduate. Developer of new techniques and co-organizer of a startup. Looking to combine my software and “hard science” expertise, to lead a team that ties soft-, hard- and wet- ware together: human augmentations, medical devices, cyborg related development.
Highlights: Management
    • Professor and Principal Investigator,  managing multiple projects involving postdocs, technicians and students;
    • CTO of Ionchance – a biotech startup based on the technology I developed;
    • Lead developer : organized and managed Scientific Gentoo (Linux) project.
Research
    • Successful scientist (over 30 publications, H-index 17, >800 total citations);
    • Developed novel experimental techniques;
    • Solid theoretical and experimental background in Math, Physics and Biology.
Software
    • regular use of Big Data and AI frameworks for data analysis and modeling  (Orange, tensorflow, R, octave; python,  numpy, scipy, pymol, gromacs, etc.);
    • Strong analytical and abstraction&design capability;
    • Robust  programming (DoD approved Ada based platform);
    • System programming (C/C++, bash and gcc toolchain as Gentoo Linux developer);
    • Develop data analysis tools.
